<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">La Chaux-de-Fonds</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">La Chaux-de-Fonds is a town in the Jura mountains of the canton of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neuchatel">Neuchâtel</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, at about 1,000 metres. Rebuilt on a grid plan after a fire in 1794, it grew into a world centre of watchmaking, and together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-locle">Le Locle</a> it is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> for its watchmaking town planning. It is the birthplace of the architect <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-corbusier">Le Corbusier</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/la-chaux-de-fonds.jpg" alt="La Chaux-de-Fonds" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MadGeographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_Chaux_de_Fonds.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
